    "display_name": "Baking Cookies",
    "long_instructions": "Now that you’ve built a prediction model, you’d like to use it in a program that lets users say how many cookies they’d like to bake and get an estimated amount of flour they’ll need.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Prompt the user to type in how many cookies they want to bake, then save that integer in a variable.\r\n2. Use the variable to calculate a predicted amount of flour needed.\r\n3. Print a message letting the user know the number of cookies and the predicted flour needed.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nIf you’re asking the user for input and you want Python to treat that input as a number, you’ll usually want to convert the input to an `int` first. You can use code like this to convert the input:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nint(input(\"Type in a number: \"))\r\n```",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Use a prediction model to predict how much flour you'll need to bake cookies.",
